Cell["\<\
If gains A and B are equal -> no high frequency terms left!
Calibration procedure: adjust gains until no more HF terms visible
Even if no calibration:  filter out the HF, and do an atan2 on the filtered I \
and Q
Neat!\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96294243533755*^9, 3.9629424969848547`*^9}, {
  3.962943140153214*^9, 
  3.9629431406058207`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"25ce9375-49a4-4222-99e8-\
46a67c047afc"],

Cell["\<\
This also provides one unexpected advantage: You can sample intermittently \
with the ADC, it doesn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t matter if you undersample! Since \
there is no critical lowpass after Q and I, it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s fine if the \
uC randomly misses a few samples now and then.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.962943141930278*^9, 
  3.962943250982321*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"93a9fa62-f92f-4212-9c22-\
d850bd9ad4b9"],

