Cell["\<\
This rotates the measurement. No problem for a static offset, but any drift \
in d\[Phi] will lead to a drift in the measurement. This is one disadvantage \
of the phase measurement method: we are sensitive to phase drifts, which can \
be a problem in a resonant transformer with high Q. (Actually, both source \
signals would drift the same amount, since they are at the same frequency, \
unless there is a differential drift in the gain stages)\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9629604912769537`*^9, 3.9629604952410088`*^9}, 
   3.962960566546966*^9, {3.962960618689534*^9, 3.962960704574601*^9}, {
   3.963313316270578*^9, 
   3.9633133474597073`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0f655d89-54d0-426c-a7b3-\
b438691fb735"],

