Cell["\<\
There is a constant-time error from dt, which shows up as a phase offset or \
maybe nonlinearity. This could be calibrated out by shifting the reference \
such that no HF remains.
If dt is noisy, then I get a phase noise error of \[TildeTilde] dt \[Omega], \
about 0.5 arcsec/ps for 2 MHz as a rough estimate. Even then, if it is \
random, I can just average a bit and it\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll be ok after a few \
averaging cycles.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96294442923168*^9, 3.962944577744128*^9}, {
  3.96294510295006*^9, 
  3.962945129778517*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d8f63581-7c43-4b6a-8350-\
433c02fcca7d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

